WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.463
Consider an agent used by a small
business.

00:00:03.463 --> 00:00:06.717
The agent is asked to summarize
yesterday's failed payments.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:12.554
The agent uses external tools such as APIs
or MCPs

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:14.306
to fetch failed payments,

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:16.158
identify the affected accounts,

00:00:16.158 --> 00:00:18.871
and retrieve relevant support tickets.

00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:20.667
Each result returns to the model

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.364
before it can choose the next request.

00:00:23.364 --> 00:00:24.814
That adds inference work

00:00:24.814 --> 00:00:26.842
and makes the next request wait.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.978
In this illustrative sequence,

00:00:29.978 --> 00:00:32.698
three requests and a final interpretation

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.279
take four model rounds.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.618
Instead of sequential tool calling,

00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:41.422
the model may write a program that calls
the three tools.

00:00:41.422 --> 00:00:44.586
Inside the program, it totals the failed
payments,

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:46.774
identifies the impacted accounts,

00:00:46.774 --> 00:00:49.294
and links them to three support tickets -

00:00:49.294 --> 00:00:51.012
without another model round.

00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:55.027
The program returns the final report.

00:00:55.027 --> 00:00:57.345
The model provides the requested summary,

00:00:57.345 --> 00:00:59.694
financial impact, and customer list

00:00:59.694 --> 00:01:03.044
while keeping raw records separate from
the primary output.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:08.439
The process is reduced from four model
rounds to two.

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:10.442
Routine work runs as code,

00:01:10.442 --> 00:01:13.927
maintaining a smaller, more focused
conversation context.

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:18.077
Anthropic demonstrated lower context use.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.736
CodeAct improved task success.

00:01:20.736 --> 00:01:22.779
Cloudflare built a compact interface

00:01:22.779 --> 00:01:25.101
to thousands of API endpoints.

00:01:25.101 --> 00:01:27.749
These results help explain why code
execution

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:29.862
is becoming part of the agent stack.

